# Devlog – March 22, 2026

## Overview
This devlog summarizes the first four weeks of development on State of Dissent a narrative-driven simulation game focused on survival, societal pressure, and personal 
relationships inside a divided city.

---

## Week One
- Implemented player camera and walking controls  
- Implemented player sprint  
- Implemented player interaction with couch and work terminal  
- Laid assets for the first two blocks: residential and commercial plaza block  
- Created the railroad blockout to outline the limits of the town  
- Implemented the day and time cycle  
- Implemented loop for interacting with couch and sleeping  

## Week Two
- Implemented the Money system  
- Implemented loop for working and earning money  
- Added text pop ups for:
  - Arriving to work too early  
  - Limiting work to once per day  
- Implemented Stress, Morale, and Stamina meters  
- Built gameplay loop connecting work, sleep, and player condition  
- Expanded world with two additional blocks completing the Union District layout  
- Performed minor UI adjustments  

## Week Three
- Implemented the Bills system  
- Implemented the World Dissent system  
- Created a News System tied to player discovery  
- Improved lighting for day/night cycle and reflections  
- Created reactive systems for:
  - Graffiti and posters based on dissent levels  
  - World props appearing/disappearing dynamically  
- Implemented automatic door closing at end of day  
- Added environmental storytelling elements tied to dissent  

## Week Four
- Expanded the shopping plaza with additional assets  
- Created Grandpa character (bedridden state)  
- Implemented interactive medicine system:
  - Pill bottle pickup  
  - Inventory integration  
  - Applying medicine to Grandpa to restore health  
- Fixed lighting shadow warnings  
- Resolved graffiti visibility issues at game start  
- Fixed bug where day advanced twice when sleeping  

---

## Current Core Gameplay Loop
At the end of Week Four, the game supports a functional core loop:

1. Wake up → Manage personal needs  
2. Go to work → Earn money  
3. Return home → Care for Grandpa  
4. Manage bills and resources  
5. Observe world changes through dissent system  
6. Repeat with increasing pressure  

